From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:37:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - save-all reports Aurora World Fabric durability

On a region thread an AWF flush only starts a commit, so save-all
flush printed "Saved the game" while AWF commits could be failing
(audit D4). The final success now goes through SaveAllFeedback: with
no AWF storage open it sends exactly the vanilla success; with AWF
storages it sends a pending line first, and for save-all flush the
vanilla success only after every storage confirmed a commit of what
the save wrote (waited for off the region threads), otherwise a
failure naming each storage that is not durable and its dirty count.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/commands/SaveAllCommand.java b/net/minecraft/server/commands/SaveAllCommand.java
index df5f736c230e865a9721d362d67a1a421b523e38..8e263603491bc251198240029c4c265f825bcb10 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/commands/SaveAllCommand.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/commands/SaveAllCommand.java
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ public class SaveAllCommand {
                         }
 
                         // now we have warned, so we can send success
-                        source.sendSuccess(() -> Component.translatable("commands.save.success"), true);
+                        dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.command.SaveAllFeedback.saved(source, flush); // SourbyCraft - AWF durability: success only once Aurora World Fabric confirmed what this save wrote
                     }
                 }
             };
